.TH SUPER-KILIX 6 "July 2026" "super-kilix 0.0.1" "Games"
.SH NAME
super-kilix \- clean-room Kitty-protocol side-scrolling platformer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B super-kilix
.RI [ --level " N" ]
.br
.B super-kilix
.RI --selftest " [seed] [ticks]"
.br
.B super-kilix
.RI { --rules-test | --input-test | --render-test " [seed]" | --sound-test | --dump-campaign }
.br
.B super-kilix
.BI --dump-level " N"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Super Kilix: The Driftway
is a native terminal side-scrolling platformer for Kitty-graphics terminals.
Kilix, an orange star-vault salvager, runs, jumps, and boosts a micro-thruster
inward along the Driftway \(em a chain of thirty-two derelict star-vaults across
eight districts of his own machine world.
.PP
Movement is re-derived from the genre's measured feel in the game's own numbers:
separate walk and run top speeds, a micro-thruster boost band, an impulse jump
with a held-versus-released gravity asymmetry, snappy skid versus soft coast, and
a right-ratcheting camera with look-ahead. Kilix carries a three-tier
phase-shell: a power block lifts him from Bare to Plated to Charged, and a hit
above Bare costs a tier rather than a unit.
.PP
Each district is four vaults \(em a Thesis opener, a Variation with a gated bonus
sub-area, an Ascent over gaps, and a Gate boss vault. A standard vault is cleared
by reaching its riser rail; a Gate's exit iris stays sealed until the district's
Vault Guardian is collapsed. Every guardian machine is dormant outside its local
activation range and shows a visible, non-lethal warning tell before it moves.
.PP
The campaign is generated deterministically as a pure function of the vault
index; every vault has a unique structural signature and a validated,
reachable route. All art is drawn at runtime from soft-raster primitives and all
sound is synthesised in memory; the game ships no asset files and needs no other
game installed. Run without arguments in a Kitty-protocol terminal to play; the
options below drive deterministic, headless operation for testing and inspection.
.SH CONTROLS
.TP
.B Left, A / Right, D
Move.
.TP
.B Up, W / Space, Z
Spring jump; the jump reaches a taller apex while the key is held.
.TP
.B Shift, K
Boost the micro-thruster from a walk into a run.
.TP
.B X, J, L
Fire a phase-bolt (as Charged Kilix).
.TP
.B P, Escape
Pause or resume.
.TP
.B R
Spend one unit and restart the current vault.
.TP
.B M
Toggle sound.
.TP
.B H
Open or close the field manual.
.TP
.B Q
Leave a menu or return to the title from pause.
.TP
.B Ctrl-C
Restore the terminal and quit.
.PP
Menus use the arrows or WASD and Enter. The game uses Kitty keyboard
press/release events when available, with a 0.30-second press-only compatibility
latch for older terminals.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --level " N"
Start vault 1 through 32 in practice mode. Practice does not change campaign
unlocks or the high score.
.TP
.BI --selftest " [seed] [ticks]"
Run a deterministic headless simulation across the whole campaign for the given
seed and tick count (default 1337 and 12000), validating every tick, and print a
PASS line.
.TP
.B --rules-test
Run the simulation, physics, collision, and campaign-validation fixtures.
.TP
.B --input-test
Test held-key and press-only input paths.
.TP
.BI --render-test " [seed]"
Write thirty-nine deterministic PPM scenes and check renderer purity.
.TP
.B --sound-test
Validate and offline-render every song and effect. Returns success even with no
audio sink.
.TP
.B --dump-campaign
Print the complete thirty-two-vault generated manifest.
.TP
.BI --dump-level " N"
Print vault 1 through 32 as an annotated semantic grid.
.TP
.B --version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B --help
Print usage and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SUPER_KILIX_DATA_HOME
Override the parent directory used for the versioned profile.
.TP
.B SUPER_KILIX_NO_PROFILE
Disable profile persistence (set automatically in every headless mode).
.TP
.B SUPER_KILIX_RENDER_DIR
Output directory for render-test images.
.TP
.B SUPER_KILIX_SKIP_PROBE
Skip the Kitty graphics capability probe for controlled integration tests.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ${XDG_DATA_HOME:-$HOME/.local/share}/super-kilix/profile.v1
Versioned, checksummed high score, deepest unlocked district, and sound
preference. Written mode-0600 via a temporary file, fsync, atomic rename, and
directory fsync; a corrupt or newer-format file is ignored.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kitty (1)
